// Pull request author: iampelumiade
// Change: new rule
// Title: OpenAI Codex CLI Approval and Sandbox Bypass Mode
// Sigma ID: a4a836c2-4612-4a56-ba67-6ac3e1e49b38
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Michael Adedeji
// Date: 2026-09-26 | Modified: -
// Description: Detects execution of the OpenAI Codex CLI with command-line options that bypass approval prompts
//   and sandbox restrictions. The "--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox" option skips
//   confirmation prompts and executes commands without sandboxing. The "--yolo" option is an alias
//   for the same behavior. This mode is intended for environments that provide an external isolation
//   boundary.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use in isolated development, testing, or automation environments where approval and sandbox bypass behavior is explicitly intended.
// References:
//   - https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/06f97622f8529feef0d230fc37519c36c6bb2eeb/codex-rs/utils/cli/src/shared_options.rs
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/16f0ad34fe5766d6d5a85d164e62a6680e859145/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_codex_approval_sandbox_bypass.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\codex.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--yolo")
